---
title: Cinnamon-Spiced Aubergines with Bulgur Wheat and Feta
source: Roasting Tin
servings: 3
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 25 minutes
---

Preheat the oven to 200°C. You will need two #roasting tins{} for this dish: trust me I've tried doing it all in just one tin, and the aubergines do not like it.

Tip the @bulgur wheat{200%g}, @vegetable stock{400%ml} and @green pitted olives{100%g} into a smaller roasting tin while you get on with slicing the @aubergine{1}(sliced into 12cm half moons) and @red onion{1}(thickly sliced).

Mix the vegetables with the @ground cinnamon{1%tsp}, @nutmeg{0.5}(grated), @sea salt flakes{1%tsp} and @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a second roasting tin, large enough to hold everything in a single layer.

Transfer both roasting tins to the oven for ~{25%minutes}, until the aubergines are crisp and cooked through and the bulgur wheat is fluffy, with all the stock absorbed.

Stir the @flat-leaf parsley leaves{25%g}(finely chopped), @rocket{100%g}(finely chopped), @lemon{1}(juice only), plus more if needed, and @extra virgin olive oil{1%tbsp} through the bulgur wheat, then taste and adjust the salt and lemon juice as needed.

Let everything cool down, then transfer the bulgur wheat into lunchboxes, top with the roasted aubergines and scatter the @feta cheese{200%g}(crumbled) and @pomegranate{1}(seeds only) over the top.

Refrigerate until needed.
